[Music]  google cloud recently announced the new  postgresql interface for cloud spanner  this combines the power and reliability  of spanner with the familiarity of  postgres  postgres is a well-established open  source database with a vibrant and  growing ecosystem that many development  and ops teams are already familiar with  the postgres interface allows  organizations to take advantage of  google's managed relational database  using standard tools and skills from the  postgres ecosystem  the interface supports spanner's rich  feature set as well as common postgres  data types and sql syntax  in this video i will show you how easy  it is to set up a spanner database with  the postgresql interface  then integrate that into a python  application using the open source  spanner client library and finally i'll  use the standard postgres psql command  line tool to explore the database  first let's create a new spanner  instance using the cloud console  i'm creating a small instance for this  test with spanner's granular instant  sizing i can easily scale that up later  as needed without downtime or  re-architecture  a spanner instance can host multiple  databases  if you already have an existing spanner  instance you will need to create a new  database with the postgres dialect  support  when i create a database i can choose  between google standard sql and  postgresql as the dialect  i'll select the postgresql option  both dialects support the same set of  capabilities  it's important to mention that the  postgres interface does not implement  all of postgres sql functionality  rather it provides postgres syntax for  existing spanner features to avoid  having to learn new semantics when you  begin using spanner  so next i will create a users table  i'll use postgres ddl and data types  because it's just postgres the schema  change would run the same in any other  postgres environment  so this makes applications written  against the postgres interface more  portable  it's worth mentioning that you can use  the gcloud command line tool to create  the database if you prefer just make  sure to specify the database dialect  option  leveraging one of the supported spanner  drivers you can start writing  applications against the database we  just created right away  besides the spanner client library no  additional software is needed  for example  we have a python application here that  connects to our database and leverages  the postgresql interface  i've downloaded the spanner python  client library and installed it via pip  into my virtual environment  in this simple application i import the  library and define the instance and  database  then i issue an insert into our users  table using familiar postgres syntax  for instance i'm not having to specify a  column list like i would with spanner's  dialect  you'll also notice that i use the  postgres now function to populate the  timestamp columns rather than the  current timestamp function available in  spanner's default sql dialect  i just showed how we could use the  native spanner driver to run postgres  syntax sql from a python application but  what about other tools like psql that  don't know anything about spanner  for those we've provided a proxy called  the pg adapter that translates the  postgres wire protocol into spanner's  own grpc based protocol  to set it up you will need to  authenticate with the gcloud command  line tool to generate the credentials  required to connect to your spanner  instance  then download the pg adapter jar file  and run it that's it  with pg adapter running the only thing  left is to connect with psql  i can use psql syntax to list out the  tables  now i can create a unique index on the  email field in our users table again  leveraging postgres syntax  next i want to query the information  schema  you can see that the postgres data types  are displayed for the columns  initially pgadapter is only provided for  development scenarios with psql but we'd  like to support a broader range of  postgres tools eventually  so that's how easy it is to set up a  spanner instance with the new postgresql  interface and get started using it in  your application and with psql  if you want google's highly available  and scalable managed relational database  and already know postgres sql syntax  this is for you  the postgresql interface for spanner is  now available for preview  you can sign up for the preview by  filling out the form in the description  below  go ahead and try it out and let us know  what you think in the comments  you

